          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What blood pressure target does guidance describe for most adults?",
          "answer": "The guidance I could retrieve does not state a specific blood pressure target for most adults.\n\nThe document \"Hypertension: diagnostic thresholds and blood-pressure targets\" says it covers \"the treatment target most bodies set once treatment has begun,\" but the part I received stops before giving that number. So I can't tell you what the target is from these results.\n\nThe same document does classify office readings for adults (US society guidance):\n\n- **Normal:** systolic below 120 and diastolic below 80.\n- **Elevated:** systolic 120 to 129 and diastolic below 80.\n- **Stage 1 hypertension:** systolic 130 to 139 or diastolic 80 to 89.\n- **Stage 2 hypertension:** systolic 140 or higher or diastolic 90 or higher.\n\nIf a reading falls into different categories for the top and bottom numbers, the higher category applies.\n\nA clinician can tell you which target applies to you, since targets can depend on other health conditions.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
